      "problem": "Disprove the following statement:\n\n$-4x-{x}^{2}\\le 0$ for any $x\\in R.$\n\nTo {{field-1}} a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a {{field-2}}. \n\nIn other words, we need to show that {{field-3}}\n\n$$\n-4x-{x}^{2}{{field-4}}0.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=$ {{field-5}} into the expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x-{x}^{2} & =-4({{field-6}})-{({{field-7}})}^{2} \\\\  & ={{field-8}} \\\\  & {{field-9}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x=$ {{field-10}} is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false.",
